    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1428">

                <pb facs="1100" n="984" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg984"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/113.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister to Mexico to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 8, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>274. Department’s 392, January 5. I referred this to Carothers on December 16 and
                    have had no reply. Besides, General Villa is reported to be in Chihuahua.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
